<!-- A file needs one document root, so the screens and the print page sit inside
     one container, the way wp_reference.olx holds the reference pages. Nothing
     mounts this wrapper: the unit's Sequential (whose_phenomenon_sba_part1.olx)
     reaches each screen by id.

     ===================================================================
     HOW THE GATES WORK (October 2026 revision; item 21 of the meeting notes)
     ===================================================================
     NextReveal has no gate of its own, and the Sequential's Next button ignores
     what is happening inside a screen. So progress is held in two places:

     1. Inside a screen. After each check, the rest of the screen sits in an
        IntakeGate whose first child is a short "do this to continue" note and
        whose second child is an inner NextReveal with everything that follows.
        ready= is the check's own condition OR the screen's latch, so a screen a
        student has finished stays open even if they later change an answer.

     2. Between screens. The last revealed step of each screen carries an
        OnShow that writes "yes" into that screen's latch (a LineInput parked in
        the Hidden block below). The next screen's <Use> in the Sequential has
        when="@wp_ok_sN.value", so the unit's Next button stays disabled until
        the screen before it is done. Latches never unset.

     The replay episodes need no latches: every fork's later content is already
     when-gated on its choice, and a chosen radio cannot be un-chosen, so the
     Sequential gates them on their own choices directly.
-->
