<Vertical id="wp_s1" title="Before you go back in">
<Markdown id="wp_s1_intro">
## Unit 1 · Investigating Matter

**Thursday, 8:30 a.m., the methods seminar room in Ball Hall.**

On Tuesday afternoon you were at the back of Room 14 at Maplewood Elementary when your cooperating teacher, Ms. Boyd, opened her new fourth-grade unit, *Investigating Matter*. With her permission, the first four minutes were recorded and transcribed for your methods course.

This morning, before you go back in for your next placement block, Dr. Okafor (your ELED 3261 instructor, who also supervises the Maplewood placements) is meeting with the five candidates placed at the school: you, Jordan, Nyota, Dwayne, and Luke. Everyone has read the transcript. Not everyone agrees about what it shows, and Dr. Okafor won't settle it for you. She'll ask you to show her.

**In this unit you will:**

- read the room before you read the lesson;
- learn the framework's vocabulary by using it;
- read those four minutes closely, against Ms. Boyd's own plan;
- argue about whose experience the launch assumed, with people who don't agree with you or each other;
- replay the launch yourself, making her decisions against the clock; and
- plan a launch of your own for the same room.

**How it works.** Click **Next** to move through each conversation. When a step asks you to do something (match terms, answer a question, write a few sentences), the conversation picks up as soon as you've done it. Your work collects in **Reference › My Launch Study**.

> 📎 **Reference**, in the menu on the left, holds everything you might want to look up: Ms. Boyd's lesson materials and the standards behind them, the class roster, the school, the research, your notes on the transcript, and your own Launch Study. The conversation will point you there when it matters. You can open it any time; clicking **Unit 1** in the menu brings you back to where you were.
</Markdown>
</Vertical>

<Vertical id="wp_s2" title="Room 14">
<NextReveal id="wp_s2_reveal">

<TalkBubble id="wp_s2_okafor" who="Okafor" face="serious" side="primary">
<Markdown id="wp_s2_okafor_md">Before we get to the lesson, here's the file I'd want in your hand walking into that room. Twenty-two kids. Four of them talk in the four minutes we recorded, and I want you to know who they are before you read a word they said. The same sentence from a teacher lands differently on each of them, and that's most of what we're doing today. Read through it, then tell me your first impression of the room.</Markdown>
</TalkBubble>

<Vertical id="wp_s2_file">
<Use ref="wp_room14" />
<Markdown id="wp_s2_file_pointer">
> 📎 This file stays in **Reference › School** and **Reference › Class roster** for the rest of the unit.
</Markdown>
</Vertical>

<Vertical id="wp_s2_impression">
<Use ref="wp_room14_impression_input" />
<IntakeGate id="wp_s2_g1" ready="wordcount(@wp_room14_impression.value) &gt;= 12 || @wp_ok_s2.value">
<Markdown id="wp_s2_lock1"> </Markdown>
<NextReveal id="wp_s2_reveal_b">

<TalkBubble id="wp_s2_dwayne1" who="Dwayne" face="calm" side="secondary">
<Markdown id="wp_s2_dwayne1_md">Twenty-six percent English learners. The district's under eight. I didn't know that about Maplewood.</Markdown>
</TalkBubble>

<TalkBubble id="wp_s2_jordan1" who="Jordan" face="serious" side="secondary">
<Markdown id="wp_s2_jordan1_md">And science is three periods a week, right after lunch, and it's the first thing that gets eaten once February hits. Honestly that's the real story on that page.</Markdown>
</TalkBubble>

<TalkBubble id="wp_s2_luke1" who="Luke" face="smile" side="secondary">
<Markdown id="wp_s2_luke1_md">Reading levels from late first grade to sixth, and the two farthest apart sit at the same table. Y'all, that's the part that would keep me up at night.</Markdown>
</TalkBubble>

<Vertical id="wp_s2_end">
<TalkBubble id="wp_s2_okafor2" who="Okafor" face="calm" side="primary">
<Markdown id="wp_s2_okafor2_md">Good. You're already reading it like teachers. Keep all of that in your head, because all of it is in play on Tuesday. Now let's get the vocabulary straight.</Markdown>
</TalkBubble>
<OnShow id="wp_s2_latch"><SetFieldAction id="wp_s2_latch_set" target="wp_ok_s2" field="value" value="yes" /></OnShow>
