<Vertical id="wp_s3" title="What a phenomenon is">
<NextReveal id="wp_s3_reveal">

<TalkBubble id="wp_s3_okafor1" who="Okafor" face="explaining" side="primary">
<Markdown id="wp_s3_okafor1_md">Ms. Boyd opens her unit with what the field calls an *anchoring phenomenon*, so before we look at her, let's get that word straight. A phenomenon is something that *happens*: an event, in a particular place and time, that you'd need to know something to explain. A topic is what the chapter's about.</Markdown>
</TalkBubble>

<TalkBubble id="wp_s3_dwayne1" who="Dwayne" face="calm" side="secondary">
<Markdown id="wp_s3_dwayne1_md">Let me back up. "The states of matter." Yesterday I'd have called that a phenomenon. Is it?</Markdown>
</TalkBubble>

<TalkBubble id="wp_s3_nyota1" who="Nyota" face="solemn" side="primary">
<Markdown id="wp_s3_nyota1_md">No. Nothing happens in it; it's the chapter title. It's a good question, though. The word was the only part that was off.</Markdown>
</TalkBubble>

<TalkBubble id="wp_s3_luke1" who="Luke" face="smile" side="secondary">
<Markdown id="wp_s3_luke1_md">Fair. But somebody still has to teach the chapter title. The kids need those words at some point.</Markdown>
</TalkBubble>

<TalkBubble id="wp_s3_nyota2" who="Nyota" face="solemn" side="primary">
<Markdown id="wp_s3_nyota2_md">Nobody said they don't. The question is which comes first.</Markdown>
</TalkBubble>

<TalkBubble id="wp_s3_okafor2" who="Okafor" face="calm" side="primary">
<Markdown id="wp_s3_okafor2_md">That argument runs through this whole unit, so let's not settle it in minute two. Start with the vocabulary.</Markdown>
</TalkBubble>

<Vertical id="wp_s3_lookfors">
<Use ref="wp_lookfors_match_problem" />
<IntakeGate id="wp_s3_g1" ready="@wp_lookfors_match_grader.correct === correctness.correct || @wp_ok_s3.value">
<Markdown id="wp_s3_lock1">🔒 *Get all six matched correctly and the conversation continues.*</Markdown>
<NextReveal id="wp_s3_reveal_b">

<TalkBubble id="wp_s3_jordan1" who="Jordan" face="cheeky" side="secondary">
<Markdown id="wp_s3_jordan1_md">Okay, "open-ended" is the one I'd have gotten wrong. So the teacher's not supposed to answer it? Like, at all?</Markdown>
</TalkBubble>

<TalkBubble id="wp_s3_okafor3" who="Okafor" face="explaining" side="primary">
<Markdown id="wp_s3_okafor3_md">Not in the first five minutes. The class keeps working on it across the unit. One quick check, then you'll put it in your own words.</Markdown>
</TalkBubble>

<Vertical id="wp_s3_topic">
<Use ref="wp_pk_topic_problem" />
<IntakeGate id="wp_s3_g2" ready="@wp_pk_topic_grader.correct === correctness.correct || @wp_ok_s3.value">
<Markdown id="wp_s3_lock2">🔒 *Find the phenomenon and the conversation continues.*</Markdown>
<NextReveal id="wp_s3_reveal_c">

<TalkBubble id="wp_s3_jordan2" who="Jordan" face="smile" side="secondary">
<Markdown id="wp_s3_jordan2_md">The maple tree got me. A tree doesn't just drop every leaf in three days. That's a "wait, why?"</Markdown>
</TalkBubble>

<TalkBubble id="wp_s3_okafor4" who="Okafor" face="explaining" side="primary">
<Markdown id="wp_s3_okafor4_md">Exactly. Now say the difference between a phenomenon and a topic in your own words. Not the list's words. Yours.</Markdown>
</TalkBubble>

<Vertical id="wp_s3_define">
<Use ref="wp_pk_define_input" />
<IntakeGate id="wp_s3_g3" ready="wordcount(@wp_pk_define.value) &gt;= 12 || @wp_ok_s3.value">
<Markdown id="wp_s3_lock3"> </Markdown>
<NextReveal id="wp_s3_reveal_d">
<Vertical id="wp_s3_end">
<TalkBubble id="wp_s3_okafor5" who="Okafor" face="calm" side="primary">
<Markdown id="wp_s3_okafor5_md">Keep that definition handy. We're about to test it against a real launch.</Markdown>
</TalkBubble>
