</Vertical>

<Vertical id="wp_s9" title="A mirror">
<NextReveal id="wp_s9_reveal">

<TalkBubble id="wp_s9_okafor1" who="Okafor" face="calm" side="primary">
<Markdown id="wp_s9_okafor1_md">Before anyone fixes anything, a mirror. Would you have picked her lake? What in your own life makes a phenomenon feel rigorous, or fun, to you? And who might that leave out? If you think I've got this whole session wrong, this is the place to say so.</Markdown>
</TalkBubble>

<TalkBubble id="wp_s9_okafor2" who="Okafor" face="serious" side="primary">
<Markdown id="wp_s9_okafor2_md">I'll go first, because I've been that teacher. My first year teaching in Lansing, I built a whole lesson around harmattan: the dry wind that comes down off the Sahara every December and turns the sky over Enugu orange with dust. I loved it. Two kids in that room could picture it. It was my lake.</Markdown>
</TalkBubble>

<TalkBubble id="wp_s9_jordan1" who="Jordan" face="cheeky" side="secondary">
<Markdown id="wp_s9_jordan1_md">I'd have picked it. Anything with a video and ice in it, I'm picking. That's probably the problem, and I know it.</Markdown>
</TalkBubble>

<TalkBubble id="wp_s9_dwayne1" who="Dwayne" face="calm" side="secondary">
<Markdown id="wp_s9_dwayne1_md">I'd have picked the river. Meeman-Shelby, my uncle, catfish. And then I'd have found out half the class has never been.</Markdown>
</TalkBubble>

<TalkBubble id="wp_s9_luke1" who="Luke" face="smile" side="secondary">
<Markdown id="wp_s9_luke1_md">I'd pick the lake again. My Wednesday-night kids at church have never seen a frozen lake either, and they'd love it. I don't think that's a problem. I think it's a window.</Markdown>
</TalkBubble>

<TalkBubble id="wp_s9_nyota1" who="Nyota" face="solemn" side="primary">
<Markdown id="wp_s9_nyota1_md">A window needs somewhere to stand, Luke. I'd still pick Saturn. I haven't decided whether that's a problem.</Markdown>
</TalkBubble>

<Vertical id="wp_s9_reflect">
<Use ref="wp_reflect" />
<Use ref="wp_self_reflect_input" />
<IntakeGate id="wp_s9_g1" ready="wordcount(@wp_self_reflect.value) &gt;= 12 || @wp_ok_s9.value">
<Markdown id="wp_s9_lock1"> </Markdown>
<NextReveal id="wp_s9_reveal_b">

<TalkBubble id="wp_s9_okafor3" who="Okafor" face="calm" side="primary">
<Markdown id="wp_s9_okafor3_md">Thanks for writing it straight, whichever way it went.</Markdown>
</TalkBubble>

<TalkBubble id="wp_s9_jordan2" who="Jordan" face="cheeky" side="secondary">
<Markdown id="wp_s9_jordan2_md">So when do we get to try it ourselves? Because I'm pretty sure I'd do it better. I'm also pretty sure that's what everybody in here thinks.</Markdown>
</TalkBubble>

<Vertical id="wp_s9_end">
<TalkBubble id="wp_s9_okafor4" who="Okafor" face="serious" side="primary">
<Markdown id="wp_s9_okafor4_md">Right now.</Markdown>
</TalkBubble>
<OnShow id="wp_s9_latch"><SetFieldAction id="wp_s9_latch_set" target="wp_ok_s9" field="value" value="yes" /></OnShow>
</Vertical>

