<Markdown id="wp_complete_md" when="@wp_completion.value.length > 0">
## Launch Study complete

You read one launch against its own plan, argued it with people who didn't agree, made its moves yourself against the clock, and planned your own. Nobody told you which trade was right. The next session asks you to design a whole activity, not around this framework, but with its principles set beside the others you know (guided practice, worked examples, time on task), and to say where they pull against each other and what you did about it.
</Markdown>

<Markdown id="wp_next_stage_md">
**Next: redesigning a classroom activity.** Not "make it AST." Take an activity you've seen taught and rework it so that a phenomenon and the children's ideas do real work in it, without giving up the guidance, the practice, and the minutes that the other half of the evidence says novices need. You'll bring the plan and the trade-offs, and this room will read it.
</Markdown>

